  "question": "Suppose $y$ is defined implicitly by $e^{xy} = x + y$. What is $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at $x=0, y=0$?",
  "answeroption": "B",
  "explanation": "Differentiate both sides:<br />$e^{xy}(y + x\\frac{dy}{dx}) = 1 + \\frac{dy}{dx}$<br /><br />At $(0,0)$: $e^{0}=1$<br />$1(0+0)=1+\\frac{dy}{dx}$<br />$0=1+\\frac{dy}{dx}$<br /><br />$\\frac{dy}{dx}=-1$<br /><br />Hence (B).",
